@node "About" "About SiL-WALL v3.ßb"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Features"}

                         - About SiL-WALL v3.ßb -

 This is a simple WALL door which should be run when a user logs in
 using the MCI Launch Door command ~CC_ in for example in the BBS:Bull.txt

 Ex:

         ---------------/STARTCUT/------
         ~
         ~CC_SiLWALL
         ---------------/ENDCUT/--------

 This version is a beta release.
 The wall is out in version v2.50 but the v3.xx I'm working on
 has many new features, most of them is ready now so I decided
 to release this as the other stuff is gonna be a bit delayed
 coded. Summertime !

 And a BIIIIIIG, HUUUUUUUUGE, MAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOR FUCK OFF to the
lame dude that used a text editor and changed the name of this door
to BIG-WALL instead of SiL-WALL and put his name in my place.

Also a fuck you to Arkadian/Infernal or was it Mel/Infernal  who got the
source code to an ealry early version of this door and then coded in a
backdoor in it and released it on some small boards.
But it's wiped out now.

So to be sure to get the the best and safest come to me directly
and get an updated, maybe registred version of all my tools.

Reachable at my board RePuLsE, addy at the end..          / The Silencer

@endnode

@node "Features" "Features in SiL-WALL v3.ßb"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Installation"}

                        - Features in SiL-WALL v3.ßb -

 This version features Relative Viewing of Quoted lines!
 That means that if a user has his NumLines set at 29 he will see
 the 22 last lines of the 100 quoted lines in the datafile.
 So if a user with Interlace or whatever and with his NumLines set
 to 60 he will see the 53 last lines of the 100 lines in the datafile!
 When the limit of 100 lines fills up it will be cut and truncated
 from the top.

                         TOOLTYPES in SiLWALL.info

                               @{"[ CHEATMODE   ]"link "Cheatmode"}
                               @{"[ LAMER.x     ]"link "Lamer"}
                               @{"[ Callerslog  ]"link "Callerslog"}
                               @{"[ Force_Write ]"link "Force_Write"}

@endnode

@node "Cheatmode" "Tooltypes"

 In the SilWALL.info there is a tooltype named CHEATMODE.
 The current setting is OFF. That means that if a User doesn't want
 to be anonymous his name will be printed after his quote in YELLOW
 color. That way nobody can 'cheat' and using the Anonymous option
 write another users handle in that place.
 But with CHEATMODE=ON the handles will be written the same color as
 the quotes which enables troublemakers to write shit and put another
 dudes handle in their place, can be quite amusing but if they start
 to write shit about the Sysop.. well :) you catch my drift!
 Check the 2 last quoted lines in the SiLWALL.iff picture to see
 what it looks like with CHEATMODE activated.
@endnode

@node "Lamer" "Tooltypes"

If you a user writes shit on the wall that you don't like, may it
be nazi or personal stuff you can easily get rid of him
by not allowing him on the wall.

LAMER.1=Borre
LAMER.2=Macroman
LAMER.3=Dracula Shark
LAMER.x= etc..

You can have as many LAMER.num as you like..
If they try to write on the wall they will get the message:

** Access Denied **
@endnode
@node "Sysop" "Tooltypes"

SYSOP.1=The Silencer
SYSOP.2=d-Zire

If you are in this list then you can write a line on the wall
in another color wich will get more attention.
You can for example write stuff conserning your board here like.
DO NOT UPLOAD BLABLA.DMS coz it's a fake or whatever.
@endnode
@node "Callerslog" "Tooltypes"

If you write CALLERSLOG=ON, Silwall will write the lines in the
Callerslog aswell. 

@endnode
@node "Force_Write" "Tooltypes"
If you wanna start from scratch on you wall you can delete the datafile
and put this feature ON.
It will then force the user of the door to write SOMETHING. hehe
There is a way out of it and that is to just press return on
the editor line.
@endnode





@node "Installation" "Installing Sil-WALL v3.ßb"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Package"}

                       - Installing Sil-WALL v3.ßb -

 To install this put the BBSCmd icon into it's place, define
 your desirable location of the door in here. Now the doorlocation
 is DOORS:WALL/SiLWALL. But you may put it wherever you like. The
 datafile for the door with all the quotes in will be named after
 the name you give the door..

 Ex.
         DOORS:WALL/SiLWALL      <- door
         DOORS:WALL/SiLWALL.dat  <- datafile

 or..    DOORS:WALL.020          <- door
         DOORS:WALL.020.dat      <- datafile

 Don't forget to name the SiLWALL.info containing the config tooltypes
 to whatever you name the door.. If you are gonna use the SiLWALL.020
 file rename the DOORS/SiLWALL.info to DOORS/SiLWALL.020.info.


 To launch this door from a bulletin file, ex BBS:Bull.txt then use
 the MCI Launch Door command ~CC_ like this...

  Ex:
          ---------------/STARTCUT/------
          ~
          ~CC_WALL
          ---------------/ENDCUT/--------
@endnode

